  "_comment_wake": "What the phone answers to. Every entry is matched FUZZILY against one- and two-word windows, which has two consequences. A short or ordinary word here becomes a wake word for half the sentences in the shop — \"hd\" and \"hedy\" were added to catch one handset's mistranscription and fired on \"hey\", \"ready\" and \"head\" instead. And an entry of three words or more can never match anything, because no window is that long. Keep entries to two tokens, long, and unlike anything a customer would say. tests/test_wake.js is the guard.",
