  "_comment_translit": "Sarvam runs in the local language and writes ENGLISH number words in the local script — \"two filter coffee\" returns as \"டூ ஃபில்டர் காபி\". A code-mixed shop counts in English half the time, so these are first-class numerals, not a fallback. Without them a quantity is simply not seen, and the line bills at a defaulted one."
